(290637, 20184, 6388, '<td valign="top">A few observations: it''s a little out of focus; you''ve cropped a fraction of the tray which looks accidental; using a table as a backdrop creates diverging lines since you''ve squared the tray with the camera - if you have to use that sort of backdrop, don''t forget that it has to be inharmony as well (not necessarily in line, it just needs to work with your subject); the glass table has both reflections and silhouettes of things underneath which is a bit distracting in my opinion.   Sorry if this seems long-winded, but lots of people have been saying they''re looking for constructive criticism, so that''s what i was going for.  good luck.  Pedro</td>', 'A few observations: it''s a little out of focus; you''ve cropped a fraction of the tray which looks accidental; using a table as a backdrop creates diverging lines since you''ve squared the tray with the camera - if you have to use that sort of backdrop, don''t forget that it has to be inharmony as well (not necessarily in line, it just needs to work with your subject); the glass table has both reflections and silhouettes of things underneath which is a bit distracting in my opinion.   Sorry if this seems long-winded, but lots of people have been saying they''re looking for constructive criticism, so that''s what i was going for.  good luck.  Pedro', '2003-05-07 12:56:12.000000', NULL, 1),
