(292923, 20674, 7010, '<td valign="top">This image meets the challenge, all right... but I''m afraid it''s not very attractive to me. I hope that I not offend you by saying this. <br/> <br/>I think the area of improvement mainly lies in the composition: cutting off the top of the object and the distracting blue ''streaks'' (window?) on the left. <br/>Other: the image is a bit underexposed, wich translates in loss of detail in the object. <br/>If I may give a tip: try to take more time for the composition of the image. Try to shoot the object from different angles. Use different materials as a background...<br/>Hope this was helpful. Regards, Marco</td>', 'This image meets the challenge, all right... but I''m afraid it''s not very attractive to me. I hope that I not offend you by saying this.  I think the area of improvement mainly lies in the composition: cutting off the top of the object and the distracting blue ''streaks'' (window?) on the left. Other: the image is a bit underexposed, wich translates in loss of detail in the object. If I may give a tip: try to take more time for the composition of the image. Try to shoot the object from different angles. Use different materials as a background...Hope this was helpful. Regards, Marco', '2003-05-09 08:53:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(292927, 20229, 7010, '<td valign="top">I like the reflection of the pieces in the ''black'' fields. You did a good job with the composition and the use of black as the bacground color.<br/>I got a few remarks, though: The pieces are slightly out of focus, and the ''thing'' behind the last chesspiece works distracting to me, also does the border of the board in the down-right corner. The pieces also got a kind of magenta color cast (is that how you call it in english?), wich I don''t like, but that''s subjective off course. Regards, Marco.</td>', 'I like the reflection of the pieces in the ''black'' fields. You did a good job with the composition and the use of black as the bacground color.I got a few remarks, though: The pieces are slightly out of focus, and the ''thing'' behind the last chesspiece works distracting to me, also does the border of the board in the down-right corner. The pieces also got a kind of magenta color cast (is that how you call it in english?), wich I don''t like, but that''s subjective off course. Regards, Marco.', '2003-05-09 09:02:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(292929, 20304, 7010, '<td valign="top">Very nice! How did you do this? Is it an aspirine, ...or a piece of CO-ice?</td>', 'Very nice! How did you do this? Is it an aspirine, ...or a piece of CO-ice?', '2003-05-09 09:04:29.000000', NULL, 1),
