(294425, 20602, 2158, '<td valign="top">This would have worked much better if you''d been on the other side of the window.  Backlighting would have given better saturation to the glass.</td>', 'This would have worked much better if you''d been on the other side of the window.  Backlighting would have given better saturation to the glass.', '2003-05-10 19:43:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(294426, 20825, 2158, '<td valign="top">Nice picture, but I can''t see what it''s got to do with the challenge.</td>', 'Nice picture, but I can''t see what it''s got to do with the challenge.', '2003-05-10 19:53:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(294429, 20674, 8202, '<td valign="top">Had it been centered better or cropped better, it has some nice qualities.</td>', 'Had it been centered better or cropped better, it has some nice qualities.', '2003-05-10 20:01:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(294430, 20779, 8202, '<td valign="top">I really , really like this.  All the reflections in the glass are perfect.  This is exceptional.</td>', 'I really , really like this.  All the reflections in the glass are perfect.  This is exceptional.', '2003-05-10 20:08:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(294432, 20771, 6660, '<td valign="top">Good idea, but I would say that it has not worked. I think that you would need a lot more glass. At the very least I would have  cleaned out the crack and tried to have filled it with as much of the green glass as possible to make it look like a proper vein.</td>', 'Good idea, but I would say that it has not worked. I think that you would need a lot more glass. At the very least I would have  cleaned out the crack and tried to have filled it with as much of the green glass as possible to make it look like a proper vein.', '2003-05-10 20:15:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(294433, 20450, 6660, '<td valign="top">My guess here is that it is a CD player lens, hence the glass. Unfortunately I cannot tell if that is the case, as it is out of focus. Would also have suggest getting really close and making that the full focus of you shot, as I do not think, anything else here helps improve it.</td>', 'My guess here is that it is a CD player lens, hence the glass. Unfortunately I cannot tell if that is the case, as it is out of focus. Would also have suggest getting really close and making that the full focus of you shot, as I do not think, anything else here helps improve it.', '2003-05-10 20:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(294435, 20679, 8202, '<td valign="top">Simple, but great.  Good color, good lighting.</td>', 'Simple, but great.  Good color, good lighting.', '2003-05-10 20:20:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(294436, 20701, 6660, '<td valign="top">This subject is probably a lot more interesting than it looks (from what I can see of the top section whichis properly lit, however the whole bottom half is in the shadows. I think it could have been really interesting if you had changed your lighting angle, and point of view. I would suggest trying to take another picture of it by putting the light from behind it, and taking your shot level or just below it, so that you can see the light streaming through - hopefully being refracted into many different directions<br/></td>', 'This subject is probably a lot more interesting than it looks (from what I can see of the top section whichis properly lit, however the whole bottom half is in the shadows. I think it could have been really interesting if you had changed your lighting angle, and point of view. I would suggest trying to take another picture of it by putting the light from behind it, and taking your shot level or just below it, so that you can see the light streaming through - hopefully being refracted into many different directions', '2003-05-10 20:20:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(294437, 20242, 6660, '<td valign="top">this type of technique has worked really well for a lot of people (take a look at some of the tutorials) however most people have used items below the glass, so that the droplets pick up and reflect the images below, creating some really fascinating and unique images.</td>', 'this type of technique has worked really well for a lot of people (take a look at some of the tutorials) however most people have used items below the glass, so that the droplets pick up and reflect the images below, creating some really fascinating and unique images.', '2003-05-10 20:22:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(294438, 20564, 6660, '<td valign="top">I think that you DOF looks good, but it is a bit difficult to tell, due to the lack of lighting. What lighting you do have (or it may be the glass) does not flatter the subject at all.</td>', 'I think that you DOF looks good, but it is a bit difficult to tell, due to the lack of lighting. What lighting you do have (or it may be the glass) does not flatter the subject at all.', '2003-05-10 20:24:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(294439, 20820, 6660, '<td valign="top">This could have been really good, unfortunately it is a bit difficult to tell due to the size of the foto. It also might have helped if you had cropped it further to loose the wooden frameworks in the top left and right.</td>', 'This could have been really good, unfortunately it is a bit difficult to tell due to the size of the foto. It also might have helped if you had cropped it further to loose the wooden frameworks in the top left and right.', '2003-05-10 20:26:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(294440, 20767, 6660, '<td valign="top">Pity about the size of the foto, which makes it really difficult to discern a lot of detail. I would suggest you sizing you foto to max sizes allowable, and then use compression to get the file size down.</td>', 'Pity about the size of the foto, which makes it really difficult to discern a lot of detail. I would suggest you sizing you foto to max sizes allowable, and then use compression to get the file size down.', '2003-05-10 20:27:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(294441, 20085, 8202, '<td valign="top">great idea for glass challenge.  Nicely done.</td>', 'great idea for glass challenge.  Nicely done.', '2003-05-10 20:28:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(294443, 20674, 6660, '<td valign="top">It likes like you were trying to pick up the blue lighting in the jug, good idea. your picture is however let down by the a lack of cropping. You really should have cropped a bit off the left so the window is out of site. If possible would also have suggested putting a black top ove the bit of light  just to the left of the jug. I would also like to have seen any reflection there would have been on the rim. Prehaps by shooting this shot as a protrait rather than landscape, might have resolved some of these issues.</td>', 'It likes like you were trying to pick up the blue lighting in the jug, good idea. your picture is however let down by the a lack of cropping. You really should have cropped a bit off the left so the window is out of site. If possible would also have suggested putting a black top ove the bit of light  just to the left of the jug. I would also like to have seen any reflection there would have been on the rim. Prehaps by shooting this shot as a protrait rather than landscape, might have resolved some of these issues.', '2003-05-10 20:31:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(294444, 20324, 6660, '<td valign="top">I see you have kept the window vertical, however there is frame? to the left which is not  - would have cropped it out as it distracts. Would also have considered another subject as there is not much else here that catches my attention.</td>', 'I see you have kept the window vertical, however there is frame? to the left which is not  - would have cropped it out as it distracts. Would also have considered another subject as there is not much else here that catches my attention.', '2003-05-10 20:34:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(294446, 20184, 6660, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately I do not find these glass items particularly eye catching. I think excluding the jug, might have improved the composition. Would also have tried to have kept out he wood edge bottom left. Srangley enough, what really does attract my attention are the reflections on the left, which look like legs, which might have made a better subject.</td>', 'Unfortunately I do not find these glass items particularly eye catching. I think excluding the jug, might have improved the composition. Would also have tried to have kept out he wood edge bottom left. Srangley enough, what really does attract my attention are the reflections on the left, which look like legs, which might have made a better subject.', '2003-05-10 20:38:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(294448, 20559, 6660, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea which i do not think has worked, partially due to the sink, which you really should have cleaned prior to this shot, as it tends to distract. I probably would also have left out the drain hole.</td>', 'Interesting idea which i do not think has worked, partially due to the sink, which you really should have cleaned prior to this shot, as it tends to distract. I probably would also have left out the drain hole.', '2003-05-10 20:40:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(294449, 20822, 6660, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, which could have been improved by getting the candles the same length, and I would have used different candle holders. The candle on the left also has too much flare and would have looked better if it had been like the middle and the right candle. But nice effect with the blue merging into purple.</td>', 'Nice idea, which could have been improved by getting the candles the same length, and I would have used different candle holders. The candle on the left also has too much flare and would have looked better if it had been like the middle and the right candle. But nice effect with the blue merging into purple.', '2003-05-10 20:42:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(294450, 20751, 6660, '<td valign="top">Would like to have seen this picture in colour as it might have attracted my attention more. Normally B&amp;W can help creative really emotive pictures, but I do not think that it has worked in this case.</td>', 'Would like to have seen this picture in colour as it might have attracted my attention more. Normally B&W can help creative really emotive pictures, but I do not think that it has worked in this case.', '2003-05-10 20:45:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(294452, 20682, 6660, '<td valign="top">Nice idea that has partly come through, but I do think that the glass lamp need a bit of cleaning as it looks pretty dirty around th top. I also looks as though it might be a bit out of focus. I know that normally it good to compose a picture using the rule of thirds, but sometimes breaking the rule can help create better pictures, which might have been the case.</td>', 'Nice idea that has partly come through, but I do think that the glass lamp need a bit of cleaning as it looks pretty dirty around th top. I also looks as though it might be a bit out of focus. I know that normally it good to compose a picture using the rule of thirds, but sometimes breaking the rule can help create better pictures, which might have been the case.', '2003-05-10 20:47:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(294453, 20233, 6660, '<td valign="top">You sure have met the subject here. Think I would have used a whiter background (or if it the light that has given the glass that pinkish glow, I would have changed it to a more natural light. Would also have cleaned up the glass and removed the browner pieces. I also would have probably kept to fewer pieces so that there was less distraction. Often simpler is better.</td>', 'You sure have met the subject here. Think I would have used a whiter background (or if it the light that has given the glass that pinkish glow, I would have changed it to a more natural light. Would also have cleaned up the glass and removed the browner pieces. I also would have probably kept to fewer pieces so that there was less distraction. Often simpler is better.', '2003-05-10 20:50:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(294454, 20686, 6660, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, which has unfortunately not worked. I think that if there had been quite a bit more glass, you idea might have worked a lot better.</td>', 'Nice idea, which has unfortunately not worked. I think that if there had been quite a bit more glass, you idea might have worked a lot better.', '2003-05-10 20:51:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(294455, 20644, 6660, '<td valign="top">Barely met the challenge, and I sort of get the feeling that the base of the glass is there so that it meets the challenge. I think you might have been better off taking the glasses from another angle, so that you got a lot more of them and their shadows.</td>', 'Barely met the challenge, and I sort of get the feeling that the base of the glass is there so that it meets the challenge. I think you might have been better off taking the glasses from another angle, so that you got a lot more of them and their shadows.', '2003-05-10 20:53:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(294456, 20441, 6660, '<td valign="top">Very nice idea, however I think you do need to have put your glass in better focus. I am also not sure about the background you have used (unless that is what has given the glass the purple fringing, but I doubt it. You probaly could have got a much better effect on a different background.</td>', 'Very nice idea, however I think you do need to have put your glass in better focus. I am also not sure about the background you have used (unless that is what has given the glass the purple fringing, but I doubt it. You probaly could have got a much better effect on a different background.', '2003-05-10 20:55:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(294457, 20166, 6660, '<td valign="top">I am sure that you intention probaly is too make everything out of focus. While the blue does help to give it a very emotive feel, unfortunately that is all it does give the picture. It might have been a lot better if some of it had been in focus.</td>', 'I am sure that you intention probaly is too make everything out of focus. While the blue does help to give it a very emotive feel, unfortunately that is all it does give the picture. It might have been a lot better if some of it had been in focus.', '2003-05-10 20:56:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(294459, 20791, 6660, '<td valign="top">Cheers for your shot. sorry could not resist. Looks as though you have picked up a TV in your glass which has also caused that rather distracting purple fringe at the top of the pic, and on the rim of the glass. I also think that you would been better off using something blue to create the effect that you have with the green. This would have helped the purple bits, and I think blue works better with red than green.</td>', 'Cheers for your shot. sorry could not resist. Looks as though you have picked up a TV in your glass which has also caused that rather distracting purple fringe at the top of the pic, and on the rim of the glass. I also think that you would been better off using something blue to create the effect that you have with the green. This would have helped the purple bits, and I think blue works better with red than green.', '2003-05-10 20:59:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(294462, 20311, 5112, '<td valign="top">Very good entry in this challenge.  B/W is a good choice.  The only thing that bothers me some is that the second from left glass looks like it''s dirty, or has a watermark?</td>', 'Very good entry in this challenge.  B/W is a good choice.  The only thing that bothers me some is that the second from left glass looks like it''s dirty, or has a watermark?', '2003-05-10 21:07:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(294465, 20496, 5112, '<td valign="top">This is my favourite entry in this challenge, even though, when I look at it, "glass" is not the first thing that comes to mind.  The colours are just beautiful.  The lighting is perfect.  My only 10 this time around.</td>', 'This is my favourite entry in this challenge, even though, when I look at it, "glass" is not the first thing that comes to mind.  The colours are just beautiful.  The lighting is perfect.  My only 10 this time around.', '2003-05-10 21:08:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(294467, 20646, 5112, '<td valign="top">I like this entry, and I particularily like the two b/w border.  IMO, for a shot of this kind everything has to be just so, perfect, completely straight, no shadows on the white background - and this one isn''t quite there, almost, but not quite.  I also think that a plain glass might have worked better than an etched glass.  It is, though, one of the better entries in this challenge. (7)</td>', 'I like this entry, and I particularily like the two b/w border.  IMO, for a shot of this kind everything has to be just so, perfect, completely straight, no shadows on the white background - and this one isn''t quite there, almost, but not quite.  I also think that a plain glass might have worked better than an etched glass.  It is, though, one of the better entries in this challenge. (7)', '2003-05-10 21:12:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(294470, 20726, 5112, '<td valign="top">A daring entry for "glass", and even though a glass object is in it, it''s not the first thing one thinks of when looking at the picture.  I think it is very interesting that you used warm tones for a picture depicting depression.  Good job!</td>', 'A daring entry for "glass", and even though a glass object is in it, it''s not the first thing one thinks of when looking at the picture.  I think it is very interesting that you used warm tones for a picture depicting depression.  Good job!', '2003-05-10 21:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(294472, 20602, 5112, '<td valign="top">I think this is a good try, but the photo would be better if it were straight, the lighting better, and the focus sharper.  I like the red of the window frame, and the colour of the bricks to the right hand side!</td>', 'I think this is a good try, but the photo would be better if it were straight, the lighting better, and the focus sharper.  I like the red of the window frame, and the colour of the bricks to the right hand side!', '2003-05-10 21:21:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(294475, 20443, 6900, '<td valign="top">I like the composition of this shot.  The reflection on the glass detracts from it, but overall it''s nice!</td>', 'I like the composition of this shot.  The reflection on the glass detracts from it, but overall it''s nice!', '2003-05-10 21:26:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(294476, 20316, 6900, '<td valign="top">Looks like metal not glass..not sure what you were going for.</td>', 'Looks like metal not glass..not sure what you were going for.', '2003-05-10 21:26:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(294477, 20212, 7711, '<td valign="top">i like how you''ve lit this. I''m not high on the glass object you chose, but you lit it well! :)</td>', 'i like how you''ve lit this. I''m not high on the glass object you chose, but you lit it well! :)', '2003-05-10 21:26:58.000000', NULL, 1),
